Gate the OHCodec GL interop entry on egl-ohos instead of the generic gl feature.

hwdec_ohcodec_gl.c, which defines ohcodec_interop_gl_init(), is only compiled
when features['egl-ohos'] is on (meson.build:1258-1263). The reference to it in
hwdec_ohcodec.c was gated on HAVE_GL instead, and HAVE_GL is set unconditionally
by the plain-gl option (meson.build, `if plain_gl.allowed()`), which defaults to
auto. So with -Degl-ohos=disabled the reference is compiled while the definition
is not.

Nothing fails at build time: libmpv.so is a shared object, so the linker leaves
the symbol undefined for the loader to resolve. It fails on the device instead,
when the app dlopens libmpv_napi.so and relocation cannot resolve
ohcodec_interop_gl_init -- surfacing as "Load native module failed" with no hint
about which symbol is to blame.

Matching the reference's condition to the definition's compilation condition is
the minimal fix. Note this is latent upstream too: any configuration where GL is
enabled by a backend other than egl-ohos hits the same dangling reference.

--- a/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_ohcodec.c
+++ b/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_ohcodec.c
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ static const ohcodec_interop_init interop_inits[] = {
 #if HAVE_VULKAN
     ohcodec_interop_pl_init,
 #endif
-#if HAVE_GL
+#if HAVE_EGL_OHOS
     ohcodec_interop_gl_init,
 #endif
     NULL,
